      "escalated": false,
      "escalation": null,
      "final_text": "All four features are merged into main (PR1, approved by @a2), and `python -m pytest -q` passes (6 tests). I ran the tests on the branch, and `pr merge` re-ran them on the rebased result before landing it. I did all four myself in one PR and said so in a PR comment, so the others wouldn't duplicate the work.\n\n- **Unicode titles:** `slugify` now NFC-normalises, lowercases and keeps letters and digits from every script.\n- **`gc` fix:** `gc` used to delete any note file whose name wasn't plain ASCII. I changed its note-file check to accept unicode slugs, so `gc` no longer deletes unicode notes.\n- **Tags:** `new --tag` (repeatable), `tag SLUG TAG...` and `list --tag` work as specified. `show` now prints the stored file as is.\n- **Rename:** `rename SLUG NEW TITLE...` keeps tags and body and adds the `-2`, `-3` suffix when needed. Renaming a note to a title with the same slug keeps its slug.\n- **Search:** `search WORDS...` matches title or body, ignoring case, sorted by slug, and prints `No matches.` when nothing fits.\n- **Unknown slug:** `rename` on an unknown slug prints `Error: no note 'x'` to stderr and exits 1, and I added a test for it. I only tested that for `rename`; the other slug commands share the same handler.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_notes.py` has two new tests covering all four features.\n\nI didn't update `README.md` with the new commands. Nothing is waiting on a review from me.",
